.TH tuuniq n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuuniq
.PP
Uniq helpers similar to Unix \fBuniq\fR, implemented in pure Tcl.
.PP
Important: \fBuniq\fR removes only adjacent duplicate lines. Sort first if you want to remove all duplicates independent of position.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tuuniq 0.2
.CE
.SS Commands
.CS
::tclutils::tuuniq::uniqList items ?options...?
::tclutils::tuuniq::text text ?options...?
::tclutils::tuuniq::file path ?options...?
::tclutils::tuuniq::adjacentCount items ?options...?
::tclutils::tuuniq::count items ?options...?
::tclutils::tuuniq::countText text ?options...?
::tclutils::tuuniq::countFile path ?options...?
.CE
.SS Options
.IP \(bu
\fB\-nocase 1\fR compare case\-insensitively
.SS Examples
.CS
set unique [::tclutils::tuuniq::uniqList {a a b a}]
# -> a b a

set counts [::tclutils::tuuniq::countFile names.txt]
.CE
.SS "Line ends"
.PP
\fBtext\fR and \fBfile\fR return text that ends with LF exactly when the input does: \fB"b\enJörg\en"\fR gives a result with final LF, \fB"b\enJörg"\fR one without, like \fBtuhead\fR, \fBtutail\fR and \fBtunl\fR. Versions before 0.2 dropped the final LF.
